cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these reference solutions, please cite them as below, and the codes and papers named per file in MANIFEST.json."
title: "Reference solutions for the LUNA hydrodynamics test suite"
abstract: >-
  Reference solutions for the test suite of the LUNA astrophysical hydrodynamics code. The repository
  collects what LUNA's tests are checked against, each file with its sha256, source code and version,
  how it was produced, the LUNA tests that read it and its licence terms in MANIFEST.json. Provided
  are: AthenaK runs from LUNA's initial conditions at high resolution (PPMX/RK4 and PLM), reduced to
  the tests' metrics, for shock tubes (Shu-Osher, Titarev-Toro, Woodward-Colella), 2D Riemann problems
  and the Liska-Wendroff implosion, Kelvin-Helmholtz (McNally et al. 2012), Rayleigh-Taylor and
  Richtmyer-Meshkov instabilities, the Gresho vortex, sound and Jeans waves, an isothermal atmosphere,
  Taylor-Green and the Evrard collapse; Arepo and mini-RAMSES runs of comoving expansion and top-hat
  collapse, and Arepo white-dwarf models and one-zone nuclear burns; AMReX Microphysics outputs
  (Helmholtz equation of state, aprox13 rates and right-hand side, screening, neutrino losses, helium
  burning, Chapman-Jouguet detonations); pseudo-spectral Taylor-Green runs and published Brachet et
  al. (1983) data; Pencil Code curves digitised from McNally et al. (2012); JAX-AMR parity outputs; a
  subset of the Timmes-Swesty Helmholtz table; and LUNA's own high-resolution outputs, which serve as
  regression references only.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Steinwandel
    given-names: Ulrich Philipp
    affiliation: "Max Planck Institute for Astrophysics"
license: CC-BY-4.0
